# Canada's population in the headlines, by province ---------------------------
# Builds one interactive HTML page: quarterly population for Canada and each
# province and territory (Statistics Canada, Table 17-10-0009-01), with news
# and government releases pinned to their dates.
#
# In the page:
#   * choose Canada or a province/territory from the drop-down
#   * switch the y-axis between population and % change year over year
#     (hover the line to see the population a year earlier and now)
#   * filter stories by source (CBC, provincial/territorial governments,
#     Statistics Canada, IRCC) and by kind (factual vs projection/plan)
#   * pick a date window (from / to month) to zoom in on a period
#   * five random headlines (each from a different year) are shown on opening;
#     tick stories in the left panel to add more;
#     headlines are placed clear of each other and the line where there is room
#
# Input:  the population numbers and the news stories, either imported from two
#   CSV files (option 1: population_data.csv, news_articles.csv) or written out in
#   this script (option 2, used as delivered). Swap the # to choose.
#   Year-over-year values start in April 2020 (a year after the first quarter here).
# Output: canada_population_headlines.html (one self-contained file), with
#   buttons to download the chart (JPEG), all references (CSV) and all data (CSV).
# Packages: plotly, htmlwidgets, htmltools, dplyr (tibble). Self-contained
# output needs pandoc, which ships with RStudio. Run in a UTF-8 session.

library(dplyr)
library(plotly)
library(htmlwidgets)
library(htmltools)

